WEBVTT

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:39.900
It's freezing cold...

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:42.720
Honestly, you're already grumbling so early in the morning.

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:45.420
What's wrong with admitting the weather's cold?

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:48.250
Did you think your grumbling would make it turn warm?

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:54.580
Then for today's snacks, I'll make something warm for you.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:56.910
I don't have class this afternoon anyway.

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:58.310
What?!

00:01:58.310 --> 00:01:59.360
That's unfair!

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:01.220
Only you! That's so unfair!

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:03.550
Um... even if you say that...

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:05.900
I've decided to go home after morning class as well.

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:08.920
Who wants to stay in school the whole day, anyway?!

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:12.830
Do as you please.

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:14.420
Hey, don't ignore me!

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:18.860
Oh? Is someone moving in?

00:02:19.850 --> 00:02:23.400
Ah, that's right, I heard a new neighbor would be moving in today.

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:46.020
Our school sure isn't cutting us any slack.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:48.410
Don't say it so happily...

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:49.800
It's impossible to finish.

00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:55.560
The holidays just ended, and they're already piling homework onto us.

00:02:56.010 --> 00:03:00.820
Oh well, I suppose it does take sheer volume to help stupid people improve.

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:04.810
I'm starting to hate studying more and more.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:09.180
Was my roundabout way of saying things too hard to understand?

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:10.760
Sorry, what did you say?

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:14.230
That may be true, but there sure is a lot this time.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:20.740
At times like this, everyone should work hard together.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.830
It's hard to do it on your own, but what if we all work together?

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:26.740
That's a good idea!

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:28.700
Then, the place where we meet will obviously be...

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:35.370
My place?

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:35.810
Yeah!

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:39.490
Chiaki's home feels so relaxing!

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:41.210
You're coming just to relax?

00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:45.660
With so much homework to do, we should probably make preparations to stay over.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:47.300
Don't just come to a conclusion by yourself.

00:03:47.900 --> 00:03:49.350
Then it's decided?

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:51.420
If we work together, it'll be finished in no time.

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:53.170
Don't just go deciding things.

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:54.330
By the way, do you mean today?

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:57.030
Thank you, Minami!

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:08.430
Well then, I'm going home.

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:10.080
It must be nice to go home.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:12.350
I guess this is what we get for being in clubs.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:13.770
It must be tough.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:15.790
Are you going to clean when you get home? Maybe do laundry?

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:19.270
I suppose... I'll do laundry first.

00:04:19.270 --> 00:04:21.510
And then crab?

00:04:22.040 --> 00:04:24.350
At this time of year, oysters aren't bad either.

00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:27.090
But I still think it can't do without chicken.

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:28.040
So?

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:30.280
What are you talking about?

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:33.520
When it comes to things to do in cold winters, it's obviously got to be nabe.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.420
Sounds good.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:39.980
Everyone bringing a secret ingredient, then turning off the lights and throwing it all into the pot.

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:44.420
Everyone will have to eat what they end up picking, even if it's a house rag.

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:46.490
Eh? That's a bit too...

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:49.600
Let's try a nabe party next time!

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:50.600
Why not?!

00:04:50.600 --> 00:04:52.270
Sounds good.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:56.910
Nabe, huh?

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:58.790
Minami Haruka likes nabe?

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:04.540
This means that Minami Haruka and I will have a nabe.

00:05:05.020 --> 00:05:08.250
That way we'll both be sweating all over.

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:11.580
I would help Minami Haruka wipe her sweat off,

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:14.410
and then for my sweat, Minami Haruka will...

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:20.050
You... are going to catch a cold.

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:23.610
Disgusting.

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:40.750
Our neighbor must've had a hard time moving in.

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:58.050
Why is this world so unfair?

00:05:58.050 --> 00:06:00.030
Huh? Uh, yeah...

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:13.340
Ah, hello.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.570
Nice to meet you, I'm Minami.

00:06:20.030 --> 00:06:24.090
Not at all, please look after us too.

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:32.320
Hey!

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:34.050
Hey!

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:38.920
That hurt!

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:40.200
That's for ignoring me.

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:42.210
I don't have time to play today.

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:44.030
I have loads of homework to do.

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:46.500
Really? So Class 1 does as well...

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:48.110
Is it the same for Class 2?

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:49.200
You come, too.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:49.860
Huh?

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:53.550
I don't get it myself, but it's been decided that we'll do homework at my place.

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:54.420
You come, too.

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:56.820
I can come along?

00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:59.370
It's more fun with more people.

00:06:59.910 --> 00:07:03.140
Don't forget our objective. We're going to do homework.

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:06.700
Bring your pajamas, because we're going to sleep over.

00:07:06.700 --> 00:07:09.640
Don't misunderstand. This is all for doing homework.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:15.630
O–Okay.

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:19.590
Oh right, I've got some good news.

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:22.030
I heard there'll be a transfer student.

00:07:22.030 --> 00:07:25.390
Boy or girl? To which class?

00:07:25.390 --> 00:07:26.770
No idea.

00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:29.150
You're so useless.

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:32.710
If it's such a good thing, then at least do some research before you speak.

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:34.590
How cold.

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:45.690
Thanks for the food.

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:47.370
That was delicious.

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:50.170
Such good zenzai.

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:54.990
And so, we're all planning to do homework together.

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:59.110
Oh? Doing homework together sounds fun.

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:02.440
Yes. Even though I still feel I was coerced into it.

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:07.810
So, can I bring four or five of them?

00:08:07.810 --> 00:08:08.650
Eh? Here?

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:09.690
Our place?

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:12.550
Everyone will be bringing their pajamas.

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:15.590
Bringing pajamas would mean... they'll be sleeping over?

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:17.370
That would be nice.

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:19.870
Thank you, Haruka-neesama.

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:23.920
Everyone staying over, huh? A pajama party?

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:26.890
No... it's for doing homework.

00:08:27.350 --> 00:08:31.270
Chiaki, pajama party is a festival from which country?

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:34.410
I don't believe it's any kind of festival, to say the least.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:37.570
When will it be happening? The Pajama Festival.

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:39.880
Today, actually...

00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:41.850
Today?

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:43.600
That's really sudden.

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:44.300
Yeah.

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:47.480
You should've given at least a week's warning for the festival preparations!

00:08:48.150 --> 00:08:50.980
It's not a festival. We're only gathering to do homework.

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:53.190
But, Haruka.

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:56.490
As the host family, we'll have to take care of them, won't we?

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:58.960
Host family?

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:00.990
I shall be the one to take charge in this event–

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:04.360
Um... So in the end, we can have it at our place, right?

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:05.210
No problem.

00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:09.640
Then I'd better start making some preparations.

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:15.470
You don't have to go, Kana. Just sit down.

00:09:15.470 --> 00:09:16.490
But, well, the preparations–

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:19.760
Don't get involved in today's gathering at all.

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:20.930
Why not?

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:25.230
Because I don't want it to get messed up by your weird ideas.

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:27.530
I'll organize this festival!

00:09:27.530 --> 00:09:30.520
If we bore our guests, then the Minami family will lose face!

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:34.520
I told you it's not a festival. We're doing homework!

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:37.520
I know, let's have nabe tonight.

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:39.100
Since many people will be coming over.

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:40.260
Great idea, nabe.

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:42.130
That's the basics for a happy family gathering.

00:09:42.130 --> 00:09:44.410
All right! Then I'll produce the cooking.

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:49.810
I'm going to buy some things. Look after the house, okay?

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:52.170
Please take care, Haruka-neesama.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:57.460
Nabe. Happy gathering. Family.

00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:00.680
Okay, then I'll go make the welcoming prep–

00:10:10.050 --> 00:10:12.720
Some new neighbors moved in next door, right?

00:10:12.720 --> 00:10:14.240
Yeah.

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:15.780
What kind of people could they be?

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:16.740
Who knows.

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:18.750
You don't want to know?

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:19.810
Not really.

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:21.190
You're so cold.

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:24.950
We're going to be seeing them from time to time, after all.

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:27.490
Don't you think it would be better to greet them?

00:10:27.490 --> 00:10:29.590
If that's what you think, then go ahead.

00:10:29.590 --> 00:10:30.500
How troublesome.

00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:37.010
In the first place, visiting and greeting is something the eldest should do.

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:38.970
So that's Haruka's job.

00:10:40.040 --> 00:10:43.010
I don't really have the right to criticize others,

00:10:43.010 --> 00:10:46.010
but don't you feel you're being irresponsible by saying that?

00:10:47.890 --> 00:10:51.840
While we're discussing this, they might actually be coming over to greet us...

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:57.410
Good evening.

00:10:57.410 --> 00:10:58.370
Evening.

00:10:58.730 --> 00:11:00.740
So it's you guys.

00:11:00.740 --> 00:11:03.010
I shouldn't have opened it.

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:04.500
Don't mind her. Come in.

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:06.210
Hi, guys.

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:08.060
Eh? Mako-chan?

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:08.880
Huh?

00:11:09.510 --> 00:11:11.750
Do you need something?

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:13.290
Come with me for a sec!

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:18.870
It's not that I don't understand your feelings,

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:20.840
but that outfit is just too awkward.

00:11:20.840 --> 00:11:22.200
Y–Yes...

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:24.960
Go and give some thought to TPO.

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:26.150
Eh?

00:11:26.150 --> 00:11:27.770
Or was it PTO?

00:11:37.390 --> 00:11:38.510
I'm back.

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:41.340
Why did she come anyway?

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:43.260
She said something about PTA.

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:44.340
What's that about?

00:11:44.340 --> 00:11:45.200
Beats me.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:48.560
So comfortable.

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:51.890
How come Chiaki's house is so relaxing?

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:53.010
Indeed~

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:55.210
Is this an alternate world for relaxation?

00:11:55.780 --> 00:11:57.890
Let me lie down a bit longer.

00:11:57.890 --> 00:11:59.800
I'm hungry.

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:02.700
Hey, this is no time to be lying around!

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:03.620
Eh?

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:06.690
Hurry up, go change your clothes.

00:12:06.690 --> 00:12:07.880
But it's only 5 o'clock.

00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:11.860
What're you saying? The festival's already started.

00:12:14.110 --> 00:12:17.110
What do you mean by festival?

00:12:17.530 --> 00:12:19.710
A festival.

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:21.360
I'm home.

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:24.110
Oh, the groceries are back.

00:12:25.210 --> 00:12:28.120
I ran into them on the way and they ended up helping me.

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:29.500
Hello.

00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:31.110
Sorry for being late.

00:12:31.770 --> 00:12:32.730
Thanks.

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:34.510
I'll go prepare dinner.

00:12:34.510 --> 00:12:36.120
I'll help you, Haruka-san.

00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:42.080
Hold up.

00:12:44.260 --> 00:12:46.870
Why are <i>you</i> here?

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:47.920
I was called over.

00:12:47.920 --> 00:12:48.650
By who?

00:12:49.300 --> 00:12:50.640
It was me.

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:54.380
Huh? But this has nothing to do with Fujioka, right?

00:12:54.380 --> 00:12:56.720
Well, we're having nabe today, aren't we?

00:12:56.720 --> 00:12:59.260
Are you someone who gets summoned by nabe?

00:12:59.260 --> 00:13:01.650
Uh, I don't think that's the case.

00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:04.660
Chiaki, what's going on?

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:09.240
Nothing really. That idiot Kana is getting fired up.

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:10.930
She even laid out a futon.

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:12.410
She sure works fast.

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:14.160
Always doing unnecessary things.

00:13:14.650 --> 00:13:16.990
Kana-chan wants to join us, doesn't she?

00:13:16.990 --> 00:13:20.190
If she wants to join in, she'll just appear when she wants.

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:21.870
I'm here!

00:13:21.870 --> 00:13:24.140
Hey, how come you guys have already changed?

00:13:24.140 --> 00:13:25.630
And a futon's even been laid out.

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:29.650
Someone would get mad if we didn't change them early.

00:13:30.300 --> 00:13:31.590
Is this everyone?

00:13:32.810 --> 00:13:36.370
What's wrong, Touma? Why aren't you changing into your pajamas?

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:38.970
I didn't bring my pajamas or anything.

00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:42.240
It's troubling that you're not in your proper attire, my honored guest.

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:44.050
Stop it, stop it!

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:46.850
Knock it off, you big sexual harrasser!

00:13:46.850 --> 00:13:49.920
Why are you so fixated on wearing pajamas?

00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:54.070
Because, you see... we're the host family, and we have to take care of our guests.

00:13:55.060 --> 00:14:00.330
Don't tell me you feel hesitant about openly joining in because it's your little sister's sleepover?

00:14:01.370 --> 00:14:02.370
Can I join you guys?

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:06.630
Can I?

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:10.640
I can, right?

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:13.640
You can...

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:17.800
Then I'll cut to the chase, 5 o'clock is too early for pajamas,

00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:19.380
even if this is a sleepover.

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:21.390
Why you...

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:30.420
The bowls... Are these the ones?

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:32.070
Yup, just use those.

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:33.450
Okay.

00:14:34.150 --> 00:14:35.300
What about these?

00:14:35.300 --> 00:14:35.790
Yes, please.

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:37.470
What is it?

00:14:37.470 --> 00:14:38.500
Nabe.

00:14:39.520 --> 00:14:41.290
The nabe's already been brought over there.

00:14:44.430 --> 00:14:46.310
All right, let's start off the nabe.

00:14:46.310 --> 00:14:48.780
I will be the one to handle this nabe.

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:51.090
Any objections?

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:55.110
First is the meat, then the fish.
Slowly put in the rest after.

00:14:56.190 --> 00:14:59.330
Hey! What're you doing?!

00:14:59.330 --> 00:15:00.810
Once you put them in it's all the same.

00:15:02.490 --> 00:15:05.320
My ideal nabe has...

00:15:06.410 --> 00:15:07.600
Chiaki.

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:08.490
Y–Yes?

00:15:08.490 --> 00:15:11.320
Put the Chinese chives and chrysanthemum greens in there too.

00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:13.320
Y–Yes...

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:17.410
Let's eat!

00:15:31.390 --> 00:15:32.420
Coming!

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:37.160
Yes? Oh...

00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:40.560
Sorry to disturb you so late at night.

00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:44.840
I just moved in next door so I thought I should come to say hi.

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:45.860
I'm Fuyuki.

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:47.710
How nice of you.
We were actually planning to visit you quite soon.

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:48.830
Is he new?
How nice of you.
We were actually planning to visit you quite soon.

00:15:48.830 --> 00:15:50.280
You're heavy.
How nice of you.
We were actually planning to visit you quite soon.

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:50.520
How nice of you.
We were actually planning to visit you quite soon.

00:15:50.520 --> 00:15:51.830
He's the eldest son, isn't he.
How nice of you.
We were actually planning to visit you quite soon.

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:52.950
He's the eldest son, isn't he.

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:53.860
I said you're heavy!

00:15:54.530 --> 00:15:57.170
Seems like a well-mannered young man.

00:15:57.170 --> 00:15:58.220
Right, Chiaki?

00:15:58.220 --> 00:16:00.120
It's about time you get off me, you idiot!

00:16:00.790 --> 00:16:03.120
Um, this is a little something from us.

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:06.660
Oh my, thank you for coming to give this to us.

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:08.970
I think it's azuki bean jelly.

00:16:08.970 --> 00:16:10.550
It's probably a towel or soap.

00:16:10.560 --> 00:16:13.070
Knock it off, you idiot!

00:16:13.210 --> 00:16:13.880
Tackle!

00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:17.210
Are there guests there?

00:16:17.210 --> 00:16:21.670
Yes... But, well, that was most likely just my sisters.

00:16:21.670 --> 00:16:24.150
If you haven't eaten yet, would you like to join us?

00:16:24.970 --> 00:16:27.530
No, it's all right.

00:16:27.530 --> 00:16:29.190
My dad has already made dinner.

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:31.650
Oh, come on! Just eat here!

00:16:32.350 --> 00:16:35.490
No, please don't worry about me. Sorry to bother you.

00:16:38.500 --> 00:16:40.540
Haruka, is he the eldest son?

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:44.480
He said only he and his father live next door.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:47.250
Oh? He seems like a pretty decent kid.

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:49.670
Is that so.

00:16:54.250 --> 00:16:55.830
I'm so full.

00:16:55.830 --> 00:16:57.960
That's unsightly, stop it please.

00:16:57.960 --> 00:17:00.430
Fujioka will see you.

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:05.160
As expected of Haruka, such perfect hospitality as a host.

00:17:05.160 --> 00:17:06.650
She didn't hear me...

00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:12.530
Don't do anything unnecessary. Everyone's here to do homework, after all.

00:17:13.060 --> 00:17:15.980
This isn't unnecessary! This is hospitality!

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:21.550
Ouch, my eyes...

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:26.250
Don't bother with Kana, or she'll only do more unnecessary things.

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:29.250
Why are you only warning me?

00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:30.450
Tell that to everyone.

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:33.250
Because you're my biggest worry!

00:17:34.470 --> 00:17:35.780
Why?!

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:39.980
Do you want to switch?

00:17:39.980 --> 00:17:42.030
Y–Yeah.

00:17:55.940 --> 00:17:57.780
Say...

00:17:57.780 --> 00:17:59.260
Yes?

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:01.040
N–Nothing.

00:18:05.330 --> 00:18:06.290
You...

00:18:06.290 --> 00:18:07.110
Yes?

00:18:07.110 --> 00:18:08.220
Look a lot like Mako-chan.

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:12.740
R–Really...

00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:19.010
Those four are taking a bath together?

00:18:19.010 --> 00:18:21.430
Was our bathtub that big?

00:18:21.430 --> 00:18:24.780
Three people at most can fit in a tub as big as ours.

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:26.510
Big...

00:18:27.760 --> 00:18:30.970
I really want a bath I could soak in more relaxed.

00:18:31.720 --> 00:18:32.720
Want...

00:18:34.060 --> 00:18:35.980
Competing to be the first to get in the bath.

00:18:36.450 --> 00:18:37.970
Competing...

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:44.200
Largeness... Wanted competition?

00:18:45.990 --> 00:18:48.410
Compete... Largeness.

00:18:48.410 --> 00:18:50.290
Want... Largeness.

00:18:50.390 --> 00:18:51.580
I'm inspired!

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:56.050
I'll show them my hospitality with... milk!

00:18:56.050 --> 00:18:59.550
I'm sure they'll drink the milk with gratitude!

00:19:01.680 --> 00:19:04.390
Haruka, what is hospitality?

00:19:04.390 --> 00:19:06.230
It's showing exquisite consideration.

00:19:06.230 --> 00:19:06.670
She didn't even give me a chance to think about it...

00:19:06.670 --> 00:19:10.050
Besides exquisite consideration, we have to work our guests up skillfully.

00:19:10.550 --> 00:19:13.260
And for that reason, I'm going to heat things up in the bath.

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:16.030
Isn't the water heated already?

00:19:16.640 --> 00:19:18.860
Hey, let's try out the new soap.

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:20.380
W–What?

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:22.530
You're looking good there...

00:19:24.110 --> 00:19:26.300
There's a dirty old man here.

00:19:26.300 --> 00:19:28.040
Get your butt out of here!

00:19:31.840 --> 00:19:34.260
I wonder who's the most 'mature'.

00:19:43.650 --> 00:19:46.130
I just heated things up in the bathroom.

00:19:46.130 --> 00:19:49.130
I'm going to have them drink this exquisite milk.

00:19:53.060 --> 00:19:54.730
Here, your cocoa.

00:19:54.730 --> 00:19:55.760
Thanks.

00:19:58.060 --> 00:19:59.630
Seems like they're getting pretty rowdy.

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:01.850
Yeah...

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:08.330
Oh, Uchida. So you've come out first.

00:20:08.330 --> 00:20:09.780
How about some milk?

00:20:09.780 --> 00:20:10.830
Thanks for the offer.

00:20:14.920 --> 00:20:16.430
One more glass.

00:20:16.430 --> 00:20:18.130
You'll get a stomach ache.

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:25.760
Oh, Chiaki. Do you want some milk?

00:20:26.060 --> 00:20:27.980
You drive me mad!

00:20:27.980 --> 00:20:29.300
What're you guys doing?

00:20:30.030 --> 00:20:31.480
Man, it's so hot.

00:20:31.480 --> 00:20:35.040
I'm thirsty. Is there anything to drink?

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:36.520
Oh? Is that milk?

00:20:37.200 --> 00:20:38.950
Do you have any fruit-flavored milk?

00:20:38.950 --> 00:20:40.260
Just go to sleep!

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:41.070
What the?

00:20:41.610 --> 00:20:43.240
Well, it's about time I go...

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:45.810
Oh, the guy without pajamas can go home!

00:20:45.810 --> 00:20:46.770
Ah, okay...

00:20:46.770 --> 00:20:48.660
Do you guys have somebody you like?

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:49.800
Do you?

00:20:51.320 --> 00:20:53.360
The night is just beginning!

00:20:53.360 --> 00:20:54.670
There's a long way to go!

00:20:55.370 --> 00:20:57.530
Cut it out already.

00:20:57.530 --> 00:20:59.160
From now on it's grown-up time.

00:20:59.950 --> 00:21:02.260
Children aren't allowed to come in.

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:05.030
What kind of basis is this?

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:06.310
What, you say...

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:15.580
The basis of having it or not.

00:21:15.580 --> 00:21:17.600
Who would accept this?

00:21:17.600 --> 00:21:19.260
Touma's a boy!

00:21:19.260 --> 00:21:21.010
What? I'm a girl.

00:21:21.650 --> 00:21:23.650
You're a boy!

00:21:24.980 --> 00:21:26.670
What is it?

00:21:26.670 --> 00:21:27.950
Not again!

00:21:27.950 --> 00:21:28.830
Jeez, let me go!

00:21:28.830 --> 00:21:29.990
She's more womanly than Chiaki, at least.
Jeez, let me go!

00:21:29.990 --> 00:21:31.070
She's more womanly than Chiaki, at least.

00:21:31.070 --> 00:21:31.980
Shut up!

00:21:32.470 --> 00:21:34.250
Enough is enough! Get to sleep!

00:21:34.250 --> 00:21:38.000
What are you saying? The Pajama Festival has just started!

00:21:39.910 --> 00:21:42.420
Time to wake up, everyone.

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:45.980
Wah, what a fulfilling festival it was.

00:21:46.500 --> 00:21:48.570
Yeah, it was fun.

00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:49.680
I want to have one again.

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:53.330
Really? I'll consider it if the idiot isn't around.

00:21:53.330 --> 00:21:54.200
What did you say?

00:21:54.930 --> 00:21:57.670
So, did everyone get a lot of homework done?

00:23:30.450 --> 00:23:32.060
Can you name all the Seven Herbs of Autumn?

00:23:32.060 --> 00:23:35.230
Bush clover, pampas grass, arrowroot, pink dianthus, patrinia, thoroughwort, bellflower.

00:23:35.230 --> 00:23:37.600
While the Seven Herbs of Spring are eaten for good health,

00:23:37.600 --> 00:23:40.610
the Seven Herbs of Autumn are plants admired in the lingering warmth of dying summer.

00:23:40.890 --> 00:23:43.050
While they aren't particularly flamboyant flowers,

00:23:43.050 --> 00:23:44.700
it's nice having such a custom, isn't it?
